# Production build values (public — client bundle, no secrets).
# The browser calls the API origin directly. api.ujimora.com allows this origin
# (CORS_ORIGINS in render.yaml) and auth is bearer-token only (no cookies), so
# nothing depends on being same-origin. Calling it directly means Cloudflare
# sees each browser's own address, which the API's per-client rate limits and
# audit trail key on; through the Vercel /api/v1 rewrite every browser shared
# Vercel's egress address. The rewrite in vercel.json stays for old bundles
# and for Preview builds: they also run in production mode and load this file,
# but their *.vercel.app origin is not in CORS_ORIGINS, so vite.config.ts
# switches every non-production Vercel build (VERCEL_ENV set and not
# "production") back to the same-origin /api/v1 rewrite. A VITE_API_URL set in
# the Vercel project for an environment overrides both.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.ujimora.com/api/v1

# No VITE_CLOUDINARY_* values: every upload goes through the API proxy
# (POST /uploads/image), which checks type and size. Setting them would put an
# unsigned-preset name into the public bundle for no benefit.
